Z||000005||Gokart||09-19-1999||07:15 AM||||Thanks guys! She's my pride and joy! The cubby under my sony I got from my Tercel. The factory stereo was so fat I needed something to support it and it fit perfect! I started with plywood with the speaker boxes (lots of cutting) then went to the boneyard and got original plastic interior from other Fieros, if you notice the grills their the same as the sides on the console in the middle! Lots of cutting as well. The woodgrain faceplates are done with simple shelfliner and top quality clear coat. Next I'm getting a replacement for my scratched drivers side window from Tom McElroy. If you noticed I got his short shifter! I'm waiting for him get some more trunk scoops and eventually I want to replace my splintered GT side windows with Fiero store's GT window scoops. Next I want to get their Mecham side scoops. I'd like to paint her yellow someday, but that will probably wait till after I replace or rebuild the engine when it goes. She's running awesome now! I got the bra from Perfect Fit Bra Co.(www.carbra.com). My other Fiero coupe I had in 92 had one and when I got the GT I got it right away. Looked naked without it! Like all bras though, it is pain in the ass to take off! <p>[This message has been edited by Gokart (edited 09-19-1999).]||||reg||14
Z||000006||GT Bastard||09-20-1999||11:35 AM||||Nice job on the wheels... Did you sand blast and paint them or what?  Powerdercoated??? It looks pretty trick.||||reg||7
Z||000007||Gokart||09-20-1999||06:54 PM||||The rims are American Racing and the polished aluminum was peeling off so I just sanded them down, primed, bombed them black then got pegasus decals for the centers and used three coats of NAPA's three part clear coat mix! I wished when I bought the car that it would've had black spider spoke rims like I had on my coupe back in 95, this is what gave me the idea.||||reg||1
